{#
  partials/_canonical.macros.twig — the page's canonical URL, shared by <link rel="canonical">
  (partials/_canonical.twig) and og:url / twitter:url (partials/_seo_metatags.twig), so both
  always name the same URL.

  Workaround for Bolt <= 6.1.10, whose canonical URL
  - names a singleton by its record route (/kontakt/kontakt-2) instead of the URL visitors
    use (/kontakt), and
  - keeps the query on a listing page (/clanky?order=-createdAt&status=published).
  https://github.com/bolt/core/pull/3735 fixes both in Bolt. Once a Bolt release with it is
  installed, delete this file, partials/_canonical.twig and partials/_seo_metatags.twig, and
  remove `canonical_template` from config/bolt/config.yaml and `templates` from
  config/extensions/appolo-boltseo.yaml.

  A canonical set explicitly (the SEO field's Canonical Link, or `override_default`) is kept
  as it is. Only Bolt's own canonical URL is corrected.
#}
{% macro url(url) -%}
    {%- set route = app.request.attributes.get('_route') -%}
    {%- if url == canonical() and route in ['listing', 'listing_locale', 'record', 'record_locale'] -%}
        {%- set definition = record is defined and record is not null ? record.definition : null -%}
        {%- set segments = url|split('?')|first|split('/') -%}
        {%- if definition and definition.singleton and segments|slice(-2, 1)|first == definition.singular_slug -%}
            {%- set url = segments|slice(0, -1)|join('/') -%}
        {%- elseif route starts with 'listing' -%}
            {%- set url = url|split('?')|first -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {{- url -}}
{%- endmacro %}
